    {
      "evidence_id": "EV-003",
      "source_file_instance_id": "9e367bf311641409",
      "page_number": 1,
      "printed_page_label": "Page 1 of 2",
      "section": "definitions",
      "section_raw": "Definitions",
      "clause_path": null,
      "exact_quote": "Definitions:\n      For the purpose of this AD, the following definition applies:\n\n      The MER: Airbus A380 Master Minimum Equipment List (MMEL), Major Event Revision (MER),\n      approval date 06 October 2020.",
      "start_char": 2111,
      "end_char": 2322,
      "page_text_sha256": "d10abd3c2e507705162c19d8d3df8c9cac0da90101079df65a80dc818e33795e",
      "bbox_normalized": null,
      "extraction_method": "native_text",
      "quality": "exact",
      "table_context": null,
      "annotation_note": null
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV-004",
      "source_file_instance_id": "9e367bf311641409",
      "page_number": 1,
      "printed_page_label": "Page 1 of 2",
      "section": "reason",
      "section_raw": "Reason",
      "clause_path": null,
      "exact_quote": "Reason:\n      Following an Airbus A380 design review for windmill relight capability in bad weather conditions, it\n      was demonstrated that handling bleed valve (HBV) failures in closed position have significant effects\n      on engine relight and engine surge margins, leading to HBV dispatch conditions that do not meet\n      the MMEL safety objective.\n\n      This condition, if not corrected, could, in case two engines are affected by this issue, lead to a\n      severe loss of thrust, possibly resulting in loss of control of the aeroplane.",
      "start_char": 2330,
      "end_char": 2878,
      "page_text_sha256": "d10abd3c2e507705162c19d8d3df8c9cac0da90101079df65a80dc818e33795e",
      "bbox_normalized": null,
      "extraction_method": "native_text",
      "quality": "exact",
      "table_context": null,
      "annotation_note": null
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV-005",
      "source_file_instance_id": "9e367bf311641409",
      "page_number": 2,
      "printed_page_label": "Page 2 of 2",
      "section": "reason",
      "section_raw": "Reason",
      "clause_path": null,
      "exact_quote": "To address this potential unsafe condition, Airbus issued the MER of the A380 MMEL that\n     incorporates temporary dispatch restrictions for MMEL item 73-25-01.\n\n     For the reason described above, this AD requires implementation of certain dispatch restrictions.\n\n     This AD is considered to be an interim action and further AD action may follow.",
      "start_char": 133,
      "end_char": 484,
      "page_text_sha256": "79af8bd0edd43cb67dba8bf530ca3f0015a385688327c301f1e169ec141268c6",
      "bbox_normalized": null,
      "extraction_method": "native_text",
      "quality": "exact",
      "table_context": null,
      "annotation_note": null
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV-006",
      "source_file_instance_id": "9e367bf311641409",
      "page_number": 2,
      "printed_page_label": "Page 2 of 2",
      "section": "required_actions_and_compliance_times",
      "section_raw": "Required Action(s) and Compliance Time(s)",
      "clause_path": "(1)",
      "exact_quote": "Required Action(s) and Compliance Time(s):\n     Required as indicated, unless accomplished previously:\n\n     MMEL Changes / Dispatch Restrictions:\n     (1)   Within 30 days after the effective date of           this AD, amend the MMEL, on the basis of which the\n           operator MEL must be made, in accordance with the instructions of the                      MER, inform all flight\n           crews, and, thereafter, operate the aeroplane accordingly.\n\n     (2)   [reserved]",
      "start_char": 491,
      "end_char": 970,
      "page_text_sha256": "79af8bd0edd43cb67dba8bf530ca3f0015a385688327c301f1e169ec141268c6",
      "bbox_normalized": null,
      "extraction_method": "native_text",
      "quality": "exact",
      "table_context": null,
      "annotation_note": null
    },
    {
